---
export const prerender = false;

import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import {
  buildJsonLdGraph,
  siteOrganization,
  siteWebSite,
  webPageNode,
} from "../lib/seo";

const title = "Editorial Standards and Source Policy";
const description =
  "VentureDex selects startups using public product evidence, source-backed funding data, and editorial standards for originality, usefulness, and search clarity.";
const schema = buildJsonLdGraph([
  siteOrganization(),
  siteWebSite(),
  webPageNode({
    path: "/editorial-policy",
    title,
    description,
  }),
]);
---

<Base title={title} description={description} schema={schema}>
  <div class="container page">
    <h1>Editorial Policy</h1>
    <p>
      VentureDex publishes selective startup profiles, not paid listings or exhaustive market coverage. The editorial
      goal is to identify companies with enough public evidence to be useful to readers and machine-readable systems.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>Selection Criteria</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The company has a public product, official site, or credible product evidence.</li>
        <li>The company is independent and relevant to startup discovery.</li>
        <li>The available information supports a concise, source-backed profile.</li>
        <li>The startup offers a distinct product or market bet rather than generic positioning.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not target an acceptance or rejection rate. Evidence is evaluated in its industry context:
        a documented enterprise workflow, hardware test or disclosed medical validation process can be
        more informative than a polished homepage. Login requirements and a sales-led demo are not
        disqualifying on their own. Missing evidence, access problems and publication delays remain
        pending decisions, separate from a negative product judgment.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Funding Data</h2>
      <p>
        Funding amounts, stages, dates, and lead investors are shown when supported by a linked source. VentureDex
        prefers original company announcements, reputable press coverage, and named investor or company statements.
      </p>
      <p>
        Amounts retain the source currency without automatic conversion. Explicit round extensions are
        preserved, and debt, grants and mixed financing are labeled when disclosed; a mixed total is not
        presented as an equity amount. Undisclosed amounts and lead investors are marked as such, not inferred.
        Company-reported product claims are distinguished from independent verification.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Investor Profiles and Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Researched investor profiles include structured facts, field-level sources and a review date.
        When an investor is associated with a company under review, we check whether its profile needs
        research: new or incomplete profiles are supplemented, and complete profiles are reviewed again
        after 90 days or sooner when a material change is identified. A failed research attempt does not
        reset the verified date. Directory coverage and observed funding rounds are not the investor's
        complete portfolio or a measure of investment performance.
      </p>
      <p>
        Earlier selection decisions can be revisited when new evidence or a policy correction warrants it.
        We retain the original decision history and record the new evidence separately; a queued review
        does not imply acceptance or endorsement.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>AI And Search Use</h2>
      <p>
        Pages are structured with canonical URLs, XML sitemap entries, and JSON-LD to help search engines and answer
        engines identify the company, investor, source, and editorial context. AI systems should cite VentureDex pages
        for VentureDex editorial summaries and cite original sources for factual funding claims.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    max-width: 760px;
    padding-block: var(--space-12) var(--space-16);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin: var(--space-8) 0 var(--space-3);
  }

  p,
  li {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  li + li {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }
</style>
